{"kind":"assert","text":"Hugh's direction, 2026-10-02: the acts of a room are declared by its application, not fixed by the platform. This supersedes the fixed seven-act design: plan section 4, `ActKind` in packages/contract/src/acts.ts, and every rule, criterion or note that assumes those seven are the only acts. The seven become the declared acts of the code-review application, one vocabulary among others. Reasons: it aligns Artroom with its dap-style goal of extensibility, and it avoids locking the platform into a vocabulary designed only for work-review processes.\n\nPriority: the Artroom work that enables declared acts comes first, ahead of the staging list in plan section 13. Lanes already under review finish as reviewed. The design request for declared acts says what this means for gate 1 (2026-10-05).\n\nSelf-hostable, which assert fdb08e72 left undefined, now means: Artroom, with declared acts, is judged a viable platform for building the artroom-jam, as its proof and as a basis for iteration. Hugh makes that judgement. Until then, jam spikes may start in ~/play/artroom-jam but none is approved (fdb08e72 stands on that point)."}